course: dictionary
lesson: 8208
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. Retired is one of them, so the sentence tells you which meaning you need. Look at who or what is being described, and what has stopped.
explain: Most often retired describes a person who has stopped working, usually because they are older: «Some retired people miss the routine, their workmates and the feeling of being useful.» The clues are routine and workmates. Retired people used to have jobs, but they do not go to work now.
explain: Retired can also be the past form of the verb retire, which means stopped for good. A thing can be retired too: «The International Space Station is planned to be retired» means it is planned to be taken out of use. In a story, «He retired to his room» means he went off quietly. In sport, a player who retires hurt has left the game because of an injury.
explain: To choose the right meaning, ask what is being described. A person who has stopped working, a thing taken out of use, a quiet place to go, or a game someone has left all give you different meanings. Then try your meaning in the sentence to check it.
fact: Retired is an adjective when it describes a person who has stopped working, usually because they are older.
fact: Retire is a verb. Its forms are retire, retires, retired and retiring.
fact: «He retired to his room» means he went off quietly, often to bed or to be alone.
fact: In sport, a player who retires hurt has stopped playing because of an injury.
fact: Useful phrases are «a retired teacher», «retired early» and «retired from», which tells you what someone stopped doing.
exercise: «Some retired people miss the routine, their workmates and the feeling of being useful.» What does retired mean in this sentence? | *People who have stopped working, usually because they are older | People who are very tired after a long walk | People who have been to a party | People who are learning to swim
exercise: In a story, «He retired to his room.» What does retired mean here? | Ran very fast | *Went off quietly to a private place | Stopped playing a game because of an injury | Left his job for ever
exercise: In a football match, a player retired hurt after a tackle. What happened? | He scored a goal and celebrated | *He left the game because he was injured | He won the game easily | He asked for a new ball
test: «A retired teacher» lives near the park. What is a retired teacher? | A teacher who is teaching a class today | *A teacher who no longer works | A teacher who has just started at school | A teacher who is painting a picture
test: Which word is the past form of retire? | *retired | retire | retiring | retires
exam: «The International Space Station is planned to be retired and guided down into the Pacific.» What does retired mean here? | *Taken out of use for good | Painted in bright colours | Given a new name | Made bigger and faster
